      "id": "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2026/oct/14/farming-insects-food-fodder-fertiliser-uganda",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2026/oct/14/farming-insects-food-fodder-fertiliser-uganda",
      "title": "[The Guardian Global Development] From black soldier flies to mealworms: farming insects for food, fodder and fertiliser in Uganda",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/4c6f44ed0f641614029e9d308d0812af6c34f351/252_0_2497_1997/master/2497.jpg?width=1200&amp;height=630&amp;quality=85&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;precrop=40:21,offset-x50,offset-y0&amp;overlay-align=bottom%2Cleft&amp;overlay-width=100p&amp;overlay-base64=L2ltZy9zdGF0aWMvb3ZlcmxheXMvdGctZGVmYXVsdC5wbmc&amp;enable=upscale&amp;s=0fbd4f088e661be45340a007379e3788\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 0.75em;padding:5px 10px;background:#f0f4f8;border-left:3px solid #7b9fc4;border-radius:3px;font-size:0.82em;color:#444;line-height:1.8;\">🌾 <a href=\"https://zirnhelt.github.io/super-rss-feed/review.html?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fglobal-development%2F2026%2Foct%2F14%2Ffarming-insects-food-fodder-fertiliser-uganda\" style=\"color:#7b9fc4;text-decoration:none;\">✏️</a></p>\n<p>Cultivating the nutritious bugs means families can raise livestock and enrich their own food, while lowering pressures on the land</p><p>A few minutes’ walk from his home in the Kyaka II refugee settlement, Kanane Bikanyale feeds black soldier fly larvae to chickens in a coop above a fishpond. The larvae disappear in a scrum of chickens. Nearby, more larvae grow in modified jerrycans, while adult flies are kept in netted boxes.</p><p>Bikanyale kept chickens before he fled to Uganda from the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC). But the cost of conventional feed and shortages of ingredients made them increasingly difficult to raise – a widespread pressure for millions of smallholder farmers whose margins are tight.</p><p>Kanane Bikanyale tends to his black soldier fly larvae in a rearing unit in the Kyaka II refugee camp in Uganda</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2026/oct/14/farming-insects-food-fodder-fertiliser-uganda\">Continue reading...</a>",
